1
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:07,679
Last time, we asked:

2
00:00:07,699 --> 00:00:08,559
The Sun!

3
00:00:08,859 --> 00:00:10,419
Every evening, it goes.

4
00:00:10,699 --> 00:00:12,569
Every morning, it comes back.

5
00:00:12,849 --> 00:00:13,579
Why?

6
00:00:13,631 --> 00:00:15,411
One, the Sun moves away.

7
00:00:16,631 --> 00:00:18,051
Two, the Earth turns.

8
00:00:19,271 --> 00:00:21,111
Three, clouds hide the Sun.

9
00:00:22,595 --> 00:00:24,105
Hold on to your answer!

10
00:00:25,977 --> 00:00:28,277
A little owl is hiding in this video.

11
00:00:28,527 --> 00:00:29,767
Can you spot it?

12
00:00:29,893 --> 00:00:33,153
It hides somewhere new each time, so keep your eyes open!

13
00:00:33,275 --> 00:00:34,385
Did you notice?

14
00:00:34,495 --> 00:00:36,085
I have my colours now!

15
00:00:36,185 --> 00:00:39,165
The creator finally had the budget to paint me.

16
00:00:39,263 --> 00:00:41,391
I am staying grey, and I love it.

17
00:00:41,411 --> 00:00:43,806
Real chinchillas are grey, you know!

18
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:45,170
And I am teal now.

19
00:00:45,320 --> 00:00:47,400
I think I look very handsome today.

20
00:00:47,526 --> 00:00:48,986
You against the Buddies!

21
00:00:49,256 --> 00:00:51,106
Lock in first with your fingers.

22
00:00:51,376 --> 00:00:53,206
One finger for every point.

23
00:00:53,787 --> 00:00:55,117
Today you'll learn:

24
00:00:55,364 --> 00:00:56,441
Day and night.

25
00:00:56,750 --> 00:00:58,170
What a cycle is.

26
00:00:58,369 --> 00:00:59,849
Cycle or not?

27
00:01:00,353 --> 00:01:01,293
Are you ready?

28
00:01:01,733 --> 00:01:02,503
Three!

29
00:01:02,883 --> 00:01:03,543
Two!

30
00:01:03,913 --> 00:01:04,563
One!

31
00:01:04,983 --> 00:01:05,703
Go!

32
00:01:07,092 --> 00:01:07,982
Round one!

33
00:01:08,292 --> 00:01:09,892
Why does the Sun come back?

34
00:01:10,182 --> 00:01:11,492
Show me your fingers!

35
00:01:14,960 --> 00:01:15,940
Locked in!

36
00:01:16,068 --> 00:01:16,798
One!

37
00:01:16,918 --> 00:01:19,148
I see the Sun move across the sky!

38
00:01:19,199 --> 00:01:23,309
Three! It was cloudy last night, so the clouds hid the Sun.

39
00:01:23,360 --> 00:01:24,020
Two!

40
00:01:24,140 --> 00:01:26,630
The Earth turns, just like my spinning globe!

41
00:01:27,434 --> 00:01:28,584
Look closer.

42
00:01:28,974 --> 00:01:31,836
This is the sky from our window, speeded up.

43
00:01:31,856 --> 00:01:35,046
First, the Sun comes up behind the blocks, and the sky gets

44
00:01:35,066 --> 00:01:35,806
bright.

45
00:01:35,976 --> 00:01:37,406
That is day time!

46
00:01:38,217 --> 00:01:40,667
Then the sky goes dark, and the lamps come on.

47
00:01:40,877 --> 00:01:43,037
That is nighttime: pyjama time!

48
00:01:43,646 --> 00:01:46,566
Look, there are no clouds tonight, and still no Sun.

49
00:01:46,776 --> 00:01:48,976
So clouds are not hiding the Sun!

50
00:01:49,890 --> 00:01:51,930
Then it is morning again, and night again.

51
00:01:52,130 --> 00:01:54,970
Day, night, day, night: it changes, and it repeats!

52
00:01:58,193 --> 00:02:00,084
But why does it keep repeating?

53
00:02:00,104 --> 00:02:01,224
Look closer.

54
00:02:02,834 --> 00:02:04,364
A globe is our Earth.

55
00:02:04,704 --> 00:02:06,174
A torch is our Sun.

56
00:02:06,504 --> 00:02:08,434
The red dot is Singapore.

57
00:02:08,548 --> 00:02:09,308
Watch.

58
00:02:09,638 --> 00:02:12,648
The torch stays still, and only the globe turns.

59
00:02:12,962 --> 00:02:15,942
The red dot faces the torch, so it is day time.

60
00:02:16,355 --> 00:02:19,465
Now it turns away, into the dark, so it is nighttime!

61
00:02:19,673 --> 00:02:22,943
It keeps turning, so the red dot comes into the light again.

62
00:02:26,070 --> 00:02:28,280
The answer is two: the Earth turns!

63
00:02:28,550 --> 00:02:29,580
Two fingers?

64
00:02:29,860 --> 00:02:31,070
One finger up!

65
00:02:31,119 --> 00:02:34,059
Scientists call this turning: rotation.

66
00:02:35,159 --> 00:02:38,969
Rotation means the Earth spins round and round, like my globe when

67
00:02:38,989 --> 00:02:39,849
I flick it!

68
00:02:39,971 --> 00:02:41,021
Yes, Momo!

69
00:02:41,223 --> 00:02:42,643
Be the little red dot!

70
00:02:42,923 --> 00:02:43,913
Shrink down.

71
00:02:44,193 --> 00:02:45,123
Quietly.

72
00:02:47,411 --> 00:02:50,471
You are a tiny dot on the Earth: Singapore.

73
00:02:50,983 --> 00:02:53,913
Your side of the Earth faces the Sun, so it is day

74
00:02:53,933 --> 00:02:54,663
time!

75
00:02:55,182 --> 00:02:58,032
The Earth turns, and you turn away from the Sun.

76
00:02:58,812 --> 00:03:01,952
Now it is nighttime, and you can see the stars!

77
00:03:02,476 --> 00:03:05,446
The Earth keeps turning, and the light comes back.

78
00:03:06,246 --> 00:03:07,316
Good morning!

79
00:03:09,116 --> 00:03:10,276
Say it with me!

80
00:03:10,985 --> 00:03:14,725
The repeated change between day and night is caused by the rotation

81
00:03:14,745 --> 00:03:15,715
of the Earth.

82
00:03:16,395 --> 00:03:18,745
This rotation takes 24 hours.

83
00:03:21,151 --> 00:03:25,231
So one full turn takes 24 hours: one day and one night!

84
00:03:25,510 --> 00:03:26,170
Let me check.

85
00:03:26,190 --> 00:03:29,450
Day changes into night, so it changes.

86
00:03:29,680 --> 00:03:32,239
It happens again and again, so it repeats!

87
00:03:32,259 --> 00:03:35,469
The same changes, again and again, like my school week.

88
00:03:35,659 --> 00:03:37,225
That is a repeated pattern!

89
00:03:37,245 --> 00:03:38,345
Yes, Basil!

90
00:03:38,615 --> 00:03:41,835
A repeated pattern of change is called a cycle.

91
00:03:43,455 --> 00:03:44,745
Say it with me!

92
00:03:45,453 --> 00:03:47,853
Cycles are repeated patterns of change.

93
00:03:48,383 --> 00:03:51,063
They happen in living and non-living things.

94
00:03:54,285 --> 00:03:57,185
My pencil gets shorter and shorter, so it changes.

95
00:03:57,385 --> 00:03:58,915
That means it is a cycle!

96
00:03:59,037 --> 00:04:00,597
Something is not right.

97
00:04:00,867 --> 00:04:03,047
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

98
00:04:03,327 --> 00:04:04,287
Hold on!

99
00:04:09,700 --> 00:04:10,830
Arms crossed?

100
00:04:11,100 --> 00:04:12,310
One finger up!

101
00:04:12,362 --> 00:04:15,862
The pencil changes, but it never grows long again, so the change

102
00:04:15,882 --> 00:04:17,182
does not repeat.

103
00:04:17,379 --> 00:04:19,629
Then look down there, at the traffic light!

104
00:04:19,829 --> 00:04:21,609
I think it is a cycle.

105
00:04:22,637 --> 00:04:23,817
Look closer.

106
00:04:24,025 --> 00:04:24,865
Green.

107
00:04:26,205 --> 00:04:26,865
Amber.

108
00:04:28,145 --> 00:04:28,885
Red.

109
00:04:30,165 --> 00:04:31,225
Green again!

110
00:04:31,638 --> 00:04:34,738
It changes and it repeats, just like day and night, so it

111
00:04:34,758 --> 00:04:36,128
is a cycle too!

112
00:04:38,808 --> 00:04:40,268
Show me your score hand!

113
00:04:40,548 --> 00:04:41,938
One finger or more?

114
00:04:42,258 --> 00:04:43,618
You beat the Buddies.

115
00:04:43,888 --> 00:04:44,918
Two fingers?

116
00:04:45,198 --> 00:04:46,208
High five!

117
00:04:46,780 --> 00:04:48,130
Did you spot the owl?

118
00:04:48,420 --> 00:04:50,640
It was on the tree outside the window!

119
00:04:50,778 --> 00:04:52,258
Here is a fun fact!

120
00:04:52,338 --> 00:04:54,988
Most owls sleep in the day and wake up at night.

121
00:04:55,048 --> 00:04:57,068
Our day time is their bedtime!

122
00:04:57,196 --> 00:04:58,476
Tell someone at home!

123
00:04:59,205 --> 00:05:01,405
Let's read today's key words together!

124
00:05:01,695 --> 00:05:02,455
Ready?

125
00:05:02,742 --> 00:05:03,762
Rotation.

126
00:05:05,312 --> 00:05:06,142
Cycle.

127
00:05:07,470 --> 00:05:08,790
Repeated pattern.

128
00:05:10,534 --> 00:05:11,474
Well done!

129
00:05:12,271 --> 00:05:13,901
The Earth is non-living.

130
00:05:14,021 --> 00:05:16,080
Do living things have cycles too?

131
00:05:16,100 --> 00:05:17,500
Good question, Momo!

132
00:05:17,800 --> 00:05:20,630
A hen, a chick and a teddy bear will show us.

133
00:05:20,695 --> 00:05:22,285
Find out in Part Two!

134
00:05:23,445 --> 00:05:24,546
Say it with us!

135
00:05:25,347 --> 00:05:26,097
Ready?

136
00:05:26,220 --> 00:05:26,880
One!

137
00:05:27,220 --> 00:05:27,920
two!

138
00:05:28,225 --> 00:05:29,400
Now you know!
